  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The acidic nature of the oxides of nitrogen can be determined by the strength of the acid formed by the nitrogen oxide in water.&nbsp;</p><p>More higher be the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ve</mi></math> oxidation number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-atom in its oxide more acidic be the nature of oxide. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>, is most acidic oxide.</p>"
  }
